  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka as Vice President of Indonesia, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has commenced formal processes to address the vacant position. This includes convening joint meetings to establish internal verification and ad hoc teams responsible for managing the selection procedure. While the political situation evolves, government ministers maintain that the national economic outlook remains stable, with growth targets for 2026 projected at 5.45%. Political parties, including the Democratic Party led by Agus Harimurti Yudhoyono, have signaled they will not nominate candidates, leaving the decision to President Prabowo Subianto. Various public figures have responded to the resignation, while observers note that investment stability depends largely on the orderliness of the transition. The former Vice President has stated he intends to remain in Jakarta following his departure from the office.",
